{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head `6f1e64261009f3719737b0a1f7947b19463b7b0d`, on main `e91cd232`. The behaviour stays, as the planner ruled in `4e97323a`: a new link in a used directory stops and sends nothing. The words now say what the directory holds and that a new link needs an empty one.\n\n**The branch.** I read `enrolKey` around the change.\n\n- The new words appear only when `device` and `pending` both hold and the pending attempt does not match the link. Agent-key and checker-key links still reach `bad()`, and a directory with a room or a finished setup still stops at the line above.\n- The branch returns before the code reads a key, signs, saves or calls the service. So \"This run sent nothing\" holds on both forms, and the scene's `posted()` shows it on the refusal form.\n- The refusal's `reason` comes from the validated record, and the next branch prints the same field.\n- The head adds no route or authority. The seal in `scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs` moves for this one file.\n\n**Next edit, not blocking.** The second form says \"To finish that attempt, run that link with --check\", and no test presses it, as the note says. By `docs/cli.md`, `--check` settles and follows the original without sending. If the original never arrived, `--check` does not finish the attempt, and only a run without `--check` continues it. So \"To finish\" claims slightly more than `--check` does. The step it names is the safe first step, so I do not hold the head. \"To read that attempt's outcome\" would match the doc.\n\n**Evidence.** The unit `~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-01-join-used-dir/` verifies against `SHA256SUMS` `a526122a…`, and holds no writable file. The gate exits 0 at `5790b1ac`, tree `a74f8f91`. The note keeps the two failed gates and says why each failed. The old-words control fails by the named assertion.\n\n**The merge after the gate.** No gate ran at this head, and I do not ask for one. The merge brings `dap verify` and J2's record, whose own gate and review stand, and the two paths it shares with this head hold edits in separate places. At this head I ran:\n\n- `device-key.scope.test.ts`: 5 passed.\n- `verify.test.ts`: 8 passed.\n- `assets.test.ts`, the Page's: passed, so the bundle still matches.\n- `security-entry-points.test.mjs`: 10 passed.\n- `check-notes`, `check-doc-links` (1003 links, 0 broken) and `check-commit-messages`: pass.\n\nThe worktree stays clean. The head touches no card path, so the rule in `0998f9ec` asks for no browser run.\n\n**Architecture.** One branch in the existing guard, and the record of the attempt does not change. It keeps a person's attempt in place, and moving it stays the person's step.\n\n**Security.** The refusal keeps its strength: the new words only replace words, before any key read or send. They name a stored reason and no secret, link or key.\n\n**Simplification.** The branch is the smallest place for this, since it splits one existing condition. The `bad()` above it stays for the other kinds of link.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6c6218197f068ec5238c01c059bfb7158f0ffbed","binding":"assigned","head":"6f1e64261009f3719737b0a1f7947b19463b7b0d","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:efbd525f8df218e553d79d035391af66f3519d48\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:dd58054656b9a026f75d1b95c184b4070eb1551d\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:efbd525f8df218e553d79d035391af66f3519d48","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}